module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.Charts.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBasicOpen.LocalSections

/-!
# Degree-one generation of the graded ring of sections over an affine open

Let `s` be a relative `Proj` situation — a scheme together with a commutative, nonnegatively
graded, degreewise quasi-coherent algebra over its structure sheaf (Tag 01NN) — and let `U` be
an affine open of its base. The graded ring of homogeneous local sections

`⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜ₙ(U)`

is then generated in degree one over its degree-zero part as soon as the homogeneous pieces are
*locally* generated in degree one: around every point of `U` every degree-`n` section is a
combination of ordered products of `n` degree-one sections.

The local hypothesis is quantified over arbitrary opens, not over basic opens, which is what a
sheafification argument produces: `Symⁿ F` is the sheafification of `U ↦ Symⁿ_{𝒪(U)}(F(U))`, so
a section of it is in the image of the sectionwise symmetric power only on the members of some
cover, and those are arbitrary opens. Shrinking a member of that cover to a basic open, and
converting the degree-one sections there into combinations of restrictions of degree-one
sections over `U`, is done here once.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.pieceModules`: the degree-`n` homogeneous piece, read as a
  sheaf of modules on the base *scheme*. The `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules` spelling is
  what carries the `Module Γ(X, U) Γ(M, U)` instance and the `Γ(-, U)` notation, and nothing
  about the sections of a homogeneous piece elaborates without it.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.pieceRestrict` and
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.pieceMul`: restriction of homogeneous sections and the
  homogeneous product, each with its codomain declared at that spelling.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.degreeOneSubalgebra`: the subalgebra of the section ring over
  `U` generated by the degree-one sections over `U`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.degreeOnePieces`: the degree-`n` sections lying in it, as a
  `Γ(X, U)`-submodule of the degree-`n` sections.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.homogeneousPow`: the ordered product of `n` degree-one
  homogeneous sections over an open.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.IsLocallyDegreeOneGenerated`: the local hypothesis.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.adjoin_eq_top_of_degreeOnePieces`: if every homogeneous piece
  is degree-one generated then so is the whole section ring. This is the direct-sum assembly.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.homogeneousPow_mem_degreeOnePieces`: an ordered product of
  degree-one sections is degree-one generated, which is the content of the whole notion.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.degreeOnePieces_eq_top_of_locally`: **the local-to-global
  step**, on basic opens, straight from
  `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top`: **the theorem.** Over
  an affine open, local degree-one generation implies that the graded ring of sections is
  generated in degree one over its degree-zero part.

## Implementation notes

**Where affineness is used, and it is used exactly twice.** Once to shrink an arbitrary open
neighbourhood to a basic open (`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.exists_basicOpen_le`), and once
for the local-to-global criterion itself, which rests on the sections over a basic open of an
affine open being a localization of the sections over the affine open — the module half of Tag
01P7. *No cohomology and no vanishing theorem is involved*, and only surjectivity of the
restriction-span map is needed, never bijectivity.

**The degree-one sections over a basic open are handled by an existing statement, not by a
localization computation.**
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.mem_span_range_restrict` already says that
for affine opens `W ≤ U` and `M` quasi-coherent every section of `M` over `W` is a
`Γ(X, W)`-combination of restrictions of sections over `U`. Applied to the degree-one piece and
`W` a basic open of `U` — affine by `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.basicOpen` — that is the
whole of the "clear the denominators" step, with no `IsLocalizedModule` bookkeeping.

**Every restriction and product identity here is proved as a term, never by `rw`.** The
homogeneous pieces are a family indexed by `ℤ` and their sections carry two spellings of the
same type (`(𝒜ₙ).val.obj (op U)` and `Γ(pieceModules n, U)`), definitionally equal but not
syntactically; a rewrite whose motive mentions the codomain dies *"not type-correct under the
`implicit` transparency level"*. `pieceMul`, whose codomain is declared at the `Γ(-, U)`
spelling, is what makes `r • _` synthesize an `HSMul` at all in the statements of its
bilinearity laws.

**Degrees are carried as `((n : ℕ) : ℤ)`.** The recursion for `homogeneousPow` multiplies on
the right, so the degree of the product of `n + 1` sections is `(n : ℤ) + 1`, which is
definitionally `((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)`; multiplying on the left would give `1 + (n : ℤ)` and force
a transport along `Int.add_comm` into every statement.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01P7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01P7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite DirectSum

universe u

namespace Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

/-- The degree-`n` homogeneous piece of a relative `Proj` situation, read as a sheaf of modules
on the base scheme. This spelling is what carries the module structure on sections and the
`Γ(-, U)` notation. -/
abbrev pieceModules (s : Situation.{u}) (n : ℤ) : s.base.Modules := s.algebra.piece n

/-- Restriction of a degree-`n` homogeneous section along an inclusion of opens, with its
codomain declared. -/
noncomputable abbrev pieceRestrict (s : Situation.{u}) (n : ℤ) {U V : s.base.Opens} (h : V ≤ U)
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, U)) : Γ(s.pieceModules n, V) :=
  (s.pieceModules n).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op a

/-- The product of a degree-`n` and a degree-`m` homogeneous section over an open, with its
codomain declared. -/
abbrev pieceMul (s : Situation.{u}) (n m : ℤ) (U : s.base.Opens)
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, U)) (b : Γ(s.pieceModules m, U)) : Γ(s.pieceModules (n + m), U) :=
  (s.algebra.mul n m).app (op U) a b

variable (s : Situation.{u})

/-! ### Restriction and the homogeneous product -/

/-- Restricting a homogeneous section from `U` to `V` and then to `W` is restricting it from `U`
to `W`. -/
theorem pieceRestrict_pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) {U V W : s.base.Opens} (h₁ : W ≤ V) (h₂ : V ≤ U)
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, U)) :
    s.pieceRestrict n h₁ (s.pieceRestrict n h₂ a) = s.pieceRestrict n (h₁.trans h₂) a :=
  (PresheafOfModules.map_comp_apply (M := (s.algebra.piece n).val)
    (homOfLE h₂).op (homOfLE h₁).op a).symm

/-- Restriction of homogeneous sections commutes with the homogeneous product. -/
theorem pieceRestrict_pieceMul {U V : s.base.Opens} (h : V ≤ U) (n m : ℤ)
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, U))
    (b : Γ(s.pieceModules m, U)) :
    s.pieceRestrict (n + m) h (s.pieceMul n m U a b) =
      s.pieceMul n m V (s.pieceRestrict n h a) (s.pieceRestrict m h b) :=
  (s.algebra.mul n m).naturality (homOfLE h).op a b

/-- The homogeneous product with zero on the left is zero. -/
theorem pieceMul_zero_left (n m : ℤ) (W : s.base.Opens) (b : Γ(s.pieceModules m, W)) :
    s.pieceMul n m W 0 b = 0 :=
  congrArg (fun f => f b) (map_zero ((s.algebra.mul n m).app (op W)))

/-- The homogeneous product is additive in its left argument. -/
theorem pieceMul_add_left (n m : ℤ) (W : s.base.Opens) (a a' : Γ(s.pieceModules n, W))
    (b : Γ(s.pieceModules m, W)) :
    s.pieceMul n m W (a + a') b = s.pieceMul n m W a b + s.pieceMul n m W a' b :=
  congrArg (fun f => f b) (map_add ((s.algebra.mul n m).app (op W)) a a')

/-- The homogeneous product is `Γ(X, W)`-linear in its left argument. -/
theorem pieceMul_smul_left (n m : ℤ) (W : s.base.Opens) (r : Γ(s.base, W))
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, W)) (b : Γ(s.pieceModules m, W)) :
    s.pieceMul n m W (r • a) b = r • s.pieceMul n m W a b :=
  (s.algebra.mul n m).map_smul_left (op W) r a b

/-- The homogeneous product with zero on the right is zero. -/
theorem pieceMul_zero_right (n m : ℤ) (W : s.base.Opens) (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, W)) :
    s.pieceMul n m W a 0 = 0 := map_zero _

/-- The homogeneous product is additive in its right argument. -/
theorem pieceMul_add_right (n m : ℤ) (W : s.base.Opens) (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, W))
    (b b' : Γ(s.pieceModules m, W)) :
    s.pieceMul n m W a (b + b') = s.pieceMul n m W a b + s.pieceMul n m W a b' := map_add _ b b'

/-- The homogeneous product is `Γ(X, W)`-linear in its right argument. -/
theorem pieceMul_smul_right (n m : ℤ) (W : s.base.Opens) (r : Γ(s.base, W))
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, W)) (b : Γ(s.pieceModules m, W)) :
    s.pieceMul n m W a (r • b) = r • s.pieceMul n m W a b :=
  (s.algebra.mul n m).map_smul_right (op W) r a b

/-! ### The degree-one subalgebra and the pieces that land in it -/

/-- The subalgebra of the graded ring of sections over `U` generated by the degree-one
sections. The conclusion `= ⊤` is degree-one generation. -/
noncomputable abbrev degreeOneSubalgebra (U : s.base.Opens) :
    Subalgebra ↥(s.sectionRingGrading U 0) (s.sectionRing U) :=
  Algebra.adjoin ↥(s.sectionRingGrading U 0) (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U))

/-- The degree-`n` homogeneous sections over `U` whose image in the section ring lies in the
subalgebra generated by the degree-one sections. That this is a `Γ(X, U)`-submodule, and not
merely an additive subgroup, is `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of`:
multiplying by a function on the base is multiplying by a degree-zero section. -/
noncomputable def degreeOnePieces (U : s.base.Opens) (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule Γ(s.base, U) Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U) where
  carrier := {a : Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U) |
    DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n a ∈ s.degreeOneSubalgebra U}
  zero_mem' := by
    change DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n 0 ∈ s.degreeOneSubalgebra U
    rw [map_zero]
    exact zero_mem _
  add_mem' := by
    intro a b ha hb
    change DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n (a + b) ∈ s.degreeOneSubalgebra U
    have h : DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n (a + b) =
        DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n a + DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n b :=
      map_add _ a b
    exact h ▸ add_mem ha hb
  smul_mem' := by
    intro r a ha
    change DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n (r • a) ∈ s.degreeOneSubalgebra U
    exact sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of s U n r a ▸
      mul_mem (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _
        (⟨_, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s U r⟩ : ↥(s.sectionRingGrading U 0))) ha

/-- A degree-`n` section lies in `degreeOnePieces` if and only if its image in the section ring
lies in the subalgebra generated by the degree-one sections. -/
theorem mem_degreeOnePieces_iff (U : s.base.Opens) (n : ℕ) (a : Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U)) :
    a ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U n ↔
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n a ∈ s.degreeOneSubalgebra U := Iff.rfl

/-- A degree-zero section is degree-one generated. -/
private theorem mem_degreeOnePieces_zero (U : s.base.Opens)
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules ((0 : ℕ) : ℤ), U)) :
    a ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U 0 :=
  (s.mem_degreeOnePieces_iff U 0 a).2
    (Subalgebra.algebraMap_mem _ (⟨_, ⟨a, rfl⟩⟩ : ↥(s.sectionRingGrading U 0)))

/-- A degree-one section is degree-one generated. -/
private theorem mem_degreeOnePieces_one (U : s.base.Opens)
    (a : Γ(s.pieceModules ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ), U)) :
    a ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U 1 :=
  (s.mem_degreeOnePieces_iff U 1 a).2 (Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨a, rfl⟩)

/-- Every degree-zero section is degree-one generated: those are the scalars of the adjoin. -/
theorem degreeOnePieces_zero (U : s.base.Opens) : s.degreeOnePieces U 0 = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.2 fun a _ => s.mem_degreeOnePieces_zero U a

/-- Every degree-one section is degree-one generated: those are the generators of the adjoin. -/
theorem degreeOnePieces_one (U : s.base.Opens) : s.degreeOnePieces U 1 = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.2 fun a _ => s.mem_degreeOnePieces_one U a

/-- The product of two homogeneous sections in the section ring is their homogeneous product.
This is the `mul_homogeneous` field of the chosen section-ring structure, with the
heterogeneous equality discharged. -/
theorem of_mul_of_homogeneous (U : s.base.Opens) (n m : ℕ) (a : Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U))
    (b : Γ(s.pieceModules (m : ℤ), U)) :
    DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n a * DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) m b =
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) (n + m) (s.pieceMul (n : ℤ) (m : ℤ) U a b) :=
  (DirectSum.of_mul_of (A := s.sectionPieces U) a b).trans
    (congrArg (DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) (n + m))
      (eq_of_heq ((sectionRingStructure s).mul_homogeneous U n m a b)))

/-- The homogeneous product of two degree-one-generated sections is degree-one generated. -/
theorem mul_mem_degreeOnePieces (U : s.base.Opens) {n m : ℕ} {a : Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U)}
    {b : Γ(s.pieceModules (m : ℤ), U)} (ha : a ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U n)
    (hb : b ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U m) :
    s.pieceMul (n : ℤ) (m : ℤ) U a b ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U (n + m) :=
  (s.mem_degreeOnePieces_iff U (n + m) _).2
    (s.of_mul_of_homogeneous U n m a b ▸
      mul_mem ((s.mem_degreeOnePieces_iff U n a).1 ha)
        ((s.mem_degreeOnePieces_iff U m b).1 hb))

/-- **The direct-sum assembly.** A section ring all of whose homogeneous pieces are degree-one
generated is degree-one generated. -/
theorem adjoin_eq_top_of_degreeOnePieces (U : s.base.Opens)
    (h : ∀ n : ℕ, s.degreeOnePieces U n = ⊤) :
    s.degreeOneSubalgebra U = ⊤ := by
  have key : ∀ x : s.sectionRing U, x ∈ s.degreeOneSubalgebra U := by
    intro x
    induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
    | zero => exact zero_mem _
    | of n a =>
        exact (s.mem_degreeOnePieces_iff U n a).1 (by rw [h n]; exact Submodule.mem_top)
    | add x y hx hy => exact add_mem hx hy
  exact eq_top_iff.2 fun x _ => key x

/-! ### Ordered products of degree-one sections -/

/-- The ordered product of `n` degree-one homogeneous sections over `U`. The empty product is
the unit of the graded algebra. -/
noncomputable def homogeneousPow (s : Situation.{u}) (U : s.base.Opens) :
    (n : ℕ) → (Fin n → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), U)) → Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U)
  | 0, _ => s.algebra.one.eval (op U)
  | n + 1, z =>
      s.pieceMul (n : ℤ) 1 U (s.homogeneousPow U n fun i => z i.castSucc) (z (Fin.last n))

/-- The empty ordered product of degree-one sections is the unit section. -/
theorem homogeneousPow_zero (U : s.base.Opens) (z : Fin 0 → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), U)) :
    s.homogeneousPow U 0 z = s.algebra.one.eval (op U) := rfl

/-- The ordered product of `n + 1` degree-one sections is the ordered product of the first `n`
times the last. -/
theorem homogeneousPow_succ (U : s.base.Opens) (n : ℕ)
    (z : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), U)) :
    s.homogeneousPow U (n + 1) z =
      s.pieceMul (n : ℤ) 1 U (s.homogeneousPow U n fun i => z i.castSucc)
        (z (Fin.last n)) := rfl

/-- Restriction carries the ordered product of degree-one sections to the ordered product of
their restrictions. -/
theorem homogeneousPow_naturality {U V : s.base.Opens} (h : V ≤ U) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), U)),
      s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) h (s.homogeneousPow U n z) =
        s.homogeneousPow V n fun i => s.pieceRestrict (1 : ℤ) h (z i) := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero => intro z; exact s.algebra.one.property (homOfLE h).op
  | succ n ih =>
      intro z
      exact (s.pieceRestrict_pieceMul h (n : ℤ) 1 _ _).trans
        (congrArg (fun w => s.pieceMul (n : ℤ) 1 V w (s.pieceRestrict (1 : ℤ) h (z (Fin.last n))))
          (ih fun i => z i.castSucc))

/-- **An ordered product of degree-one sections is degree-one generated.** -/
theorem homogeneousPow_mem_degreeOnePieces (U : s.base.Opens) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), U)),
      s.homogeneousPow U n z ∈ s.degreeOnePieces U n := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero => intro z; exact s.mem_degreeOnePieces_zero U _
  | succ n ih => intro z; exact s.mul_mem_degreeOnePieces U (ih _) (s.mem_degreeOnePieces_one U _)

/-! ### Spans of restrictions -/

/-- Restriction carries a span of a set into the span of the restricted set. Restriction is
only *semilinear* — the scalars restrict too — so this is not the image of a linear map. -/
theorem pieceRestrict_mem_span (n : ℤ) {U V : s.base.Opens} (h : V ≤ U)
    (S : Set Γ(s.pieceModules n, U))
    {a : Γ(s.pieceModules n, U)} (ha : a ∈ Submodule.span Γ(s.base, U) S) :
    s.pieceRestrict n h a ∈ Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V) (s.pieceRestrict n h '' S) := by
  induction ha using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx => exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  | zero =>
      have h0 : s.pieceRestrict n h 0 = 0 := map_zero _
      exact h0 ▸ Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add x y _ _ hx hy =>
      have h1 : s.pieceRestrict n h (x + y) =
          s.pieceRestrict n h x + s.pieceRestrict n h y := map_add _ x y
      exact h1 ▸ Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy
  | smul r x _ hx =>
      have h2 : s.pieceRestrict n h (r • x) =
          s.base.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op r • s.pieceRestrict n h x :=
        Scheme.Modules.map_smul (s.pieceModules n) (homOfLE h) r x
      exact h2 ▸ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hx

/-- A combination of restrictions times a combination of restrictions is a combination of
restrictions of products. -/
theorem pieceMul_mem_span_image {U V : s.base.Opens} (h : V ≤ U) (n m : ℤ)
    (A : Set Γ(s.pieceModules n, U)) (B : Set Γ(s.pieceModules m, U))
    (C : Set Γ(s.pieceModules (n + m), U))
    (hAB : ∀ a ∈ A, ∀ b ∈ B, s.pieceMul n m U a b ∈ C)
    {x : Γ(s.pieceModules n, V)}
    (hx : x ∈ Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V) (s.pieceRestrict n h '' A)) :
    ∀ y ∈ Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V) (s.pieceRestrict m h '' B),
      s.pieceMul n m V x y ∈
        Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V) (s.pieceRestrict (n + m) h '' C) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := hx
      intro y hy
      induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
      | mem y hy =>
          obtain ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩ := hy
          exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨_, hAB a ha b hb, s.pieceRestrict_pieceMul h n m a b⟩
      | zero => exact s.pieceMul_zero_right n m V _ ▸ Submodule.zero_mem _
      | add y y' _ _ hy hy' =>
          exact s.pieceMul_add_right n m V _ y y' ▸ Submodule.add_mem _ hy hy'
      | smul r y _ hy =>
          exact s.pieceMul_smul_right n m V r _ y ▸ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hy
  | zero => intro y _; exact s.pieceMul_zero_left n m V y ▸ Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add x x' _ _ hx hx' =>
      intro y hy
      exact s.pieceMul_add_left n m V x x' y ▸ Submodule.add_mem _ (hx y hy) (hx' y hy)
  | smul r x _ hx =>
      intro y hy
      exact s.pieceMul_smul_left n m V r x y ▸ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hx y hy)

/-- **The degree-one sections over an affine subopen are combinations of restrictions.** This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.mem_span_range_restrict` at the degree-one
piece, with the range written as the image of the whole degree-one submodule. -/
theorem degreeOne_mem_span_restrict (U : s.base.Opens) {V : s.base.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (h : V ≤ U)
    (y : Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), V)) :
    y ∈ Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V) (s.pieceRestrict (1 : ℤ) h '' (s.degreeOnePieces U 1)) := by
  have hy := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.mem_span_range_restrict
    (s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ)) hV hU h y
  rw [s.degreeOnePieces_one U]
  simpa [Set.image_univ] using hy

/-- **An ordered product of degree-one sections over an affine subopen is a combination of
restrictions of degree-one-generated sections over the affine open.** -/
theorem homogeneousPow_mem_span_restrict (U : s.base.Opens) {V : s.base.Opens}
    (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (h : V ≤ U) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (z : Fin n → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), V)),
      s.homogeneousPow V n z ∈
        Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V)
          (s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) h '' (s.degreeOnePieces U n)) := by
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
      intro z
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨s.algebra.one.eval (op U), s.mem_degreeOnePieces_zero U _,
        s.algebra.one.property (homOfLE h).op⟩
  | succ n ih =>
      intro z
      exact s.pieceMul_mem_span_image h (n : ℤ) 1 _ _ _
        (fun _ ha _ hb => s.mul_mem_degreeOnePieces U ha hb) (ih fun i => z i.castSucc)
        (z (Fin.last n)) (s.degreeOne_mem_span_restrict U hU hV h _)

/-! ### The criterion -/

/-- **A relative `Proj` situation locally generated in degree one over an open `U`.** Around
every point of `U`, every degree-`n` homogeneous section is a combination of ordered products of
`n` degree-one sections.

The neighbourhood is an arbitrary open, not a basic open: that is what a sheafification
argument produces, and shrinking it is part of the criterion below. -/
def IsLocallyDegreeOneGenerated (s : Situation.{u}) (U : s.base.Opens) : Prop :=
  ∀ (n : ℕ) (a : Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U)), ∀ x ∈ U,
    ∃ (V : s.base.Opens) (h : V ≤ U), x ∈ V ∧
      s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) h a ∈ Submodule.span Γ(s.base, V)
        (Set.range fun z : Fin n → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), V) => s.homogeneousPow V n z)

/-- **The local-to-global step**, on basic opens: a degree-`n` section that lies, around each
point of an affine open, in the span of the restrictions of the degree-one-generated sections,
is itself degree-one generated. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict` at the degree-`n` piece, whose
quasi-coherence is a field of the situation. -/
theorem degreeOnePieces_eq_top_of_locally (U : s.base.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (n : ℕ)
    (h : ∀ a : Γ(s.pieceModules (n : ℤ), U), ∀ x ∈ U, ∃ g : Γ(s.base, U),
      x ∈ s.base.basicOpen g ∧
        s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) (s.base.basicOpen_le g) a ∈
          Submodule.span Γ(s.base, s.base.basicOpen g)
            (s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) (s.base.basicOpen_le g) '' (s.degreeOnePieces U n))) :
    s.degreeOnePieces U n = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.2 fun a _ =>
    AlgebraicGeometry.mem_of_locally_mem_span_restrict (s.pieceModules (n : ℤ)) hU
      (s.degreeOnePieces U n) a (h a)

/-- **Over an affine open, local degree-one generation implies degree-one generation.** The
graded ring of homogeneous local sections over an affine open of a relative `Proj` situation
which is locally generated in degree one is generated in degree one over its degree-zero
part. -/
theorem adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top (U : s.base.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hgen : s.IsLocallyDegreeOneGenerated U) :
    Algebra.adjoin ↥(s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
      (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) = ⊤ := by
  refine s.adjoin_eq_top_of_degreeOnePieces U fun n => ?_
  refine s.degreeOnePieces_eq_top_of_locally U hU n fun a x hx => ?_
  obtain ⟨V, hVU, hxV, hspan⟩ := hgen n a x hx
  obtain ⟨g, hgV, hxg⟩ := hU.exists_basicOpen_le (⟨x, hxV⟩ : V) hx
  refine ⟨g, hxg, ?_⟩
  have h1 := s.pieceRestrict_mem_span (n : ℤ) hgV _ hspan
  have h2 : Submodule.span Γ(s.base, s.base.basicOpen g)
        (s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) hgV ''
          Set.range fun z : Fin n → Γ(s.pieceModules (1 : ℤ), V) => s.homogeneousPow V n z) ≤
      Submodule.span Γ(s.base, s.base.basicOpen g)
        (s.pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) (s.base.basicOpen_le g) '' (s.degreeOnePieces U n)) := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro - ⟨-, ⟨z, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    rw [s.homogeneousPow_naturality hgV n z]
    exact s.homogeneousPow_mem_span_restrict U hU (hU.basicOpen g) (s.base.basicOpen_le g) n _
  have h3 := h2 h1
  rwa [s.pieceRestrict_pieceRestrict (n : ℤ) hgV hVU a] at h3

end Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

end
